## Deviations

None — implemented exactly as specified.

## Manual verification notes

- Desktop holdings panel: ISIN, Status, Type, Shares, Avg price, Realized P&L render without truncation; short fields no longer sit in oversized boxes.
- Mobile portrait: fields wrap to fewer per row (2 on narrow) without clipping.
- Snapshot panel: per-account balance rows still read clearly under auto-fit sizing — no regression from previous fixed 2-column layout.
- Panel background/corners/padding visually unchanged.
- `.hold-detail-isin` monospace value no longer looks cramped relative to adjacent short fields.

# Description

The pgoutput streaming/CDC decoder decoded boolean columns with `data[0] != 0`. Since pgoutput streams column values in **text** format, a boolean arrives as ASCII `"t"` (0x74) or `"f"` (0x66) — both non-zero — so every streamed boolean decoded as `true`. Boolean flips (`true → false`) were never observed downstream, and queries like `WHERE flag = false` never matched on streamed changes. Bootstrap/snapshot was unaffected (it uses tokio-postgres typed access), making the bug easy to miss.

Changes in `components/sources/postgres/src/decoder.rs`:

- **Bool decode fix**: the OID 16 arm in `decode_column_value` now parses the text representation, tolerating the binary form, mirroring the neighbouring integer/float arms. Accepted inputs are restricted to exactly what pgoutput emits (`t`/`f`, `true`/`false`) plus a defensive binary `0x01`/`0x00` fallback; any other payload returns an error (reporting only the byte length, not the raw bytes):

  ```rust
  16 => {
      let value = match data {
          b"t" | b"true" => true,
          b"f" | b"false" => false,
          [1] => true,
          [0] => false,
          other => {
              return Err(anyhow!(
                  "Failed to parse bool: unexpected bytes (len={})",
                  other.len()
              ))
          }
      };
      Ok(PostgresValue::Bool(value))
  }
  ```

- **Regression tests**: added unit coverage for text `t`/`true`, text `f`/`false`, binary `0x01`/`0x00` fallback, and invalid input (empty slice, uppercase `T`/`TRUE`, SQL-only literals `y`/`1`, and out-of-range binary `0x02` — all now error instead of silently decoding as `true`).

- **End-to-end test**: added `test_boolean_datatype_bootstrap_and_cdc` (Docker/testcontainers) exercising boolean decoding across **both** the bootstrap snapshot path and the pgoutput CDC streaming path (INSERT of `false`, and a `true → false` UPDATE flip).

- **Test infrastructure fix**: added the missing `#[test]` attribute to `test_decode_timestamptz_text_no_fractional_seconds`, which was previously inert and never executed as a test.

